            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a001855</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 48-year-old man complaining of pain in his hands. In a first step, a two-sided carpal tunnel syndrome was found, and in the further course of the disease an acromegaly. The combinations of carpal tunnel syndrome, impaired glucose tolerance and radiological findings in the area of the sella turcica were the clues for the diagnosis of acromegaly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
